# Normalize line endings in the repository. Every text file is stored with LF;
# Git converts to CRLF only in the working tree on Windows if the user has
# core.autocrlf=true. Without this, a Windows checkout rewrites files on
# commit and produces diffs where every line looks changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch and PowerShell scripts must keep CRLF, or cmd.exe and some PowerShell
# hosts mis-parse their last line.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets. Marking these stops Git from attempting text conversion and
# from printing binary blobs in diffs and merge conflicts.
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.msi binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.zip binary

# Lockfiles: generated, and merging them line by line is never meaningful.
*pnpm-lock.yaml -diff
